#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
hd2-macro - one virtual Xbox 360 pad, with macro sequences, for Xbox Cloud Gaming.

Creates a uinput device byte-identical to a wired Xbox 360 controller
(045e:028e) so Chromium maps it to the W3C "standard" gamepad layout, which is
what xbox.com/play requires. Keyboard hotkeys fire configurable macro sequences
(Helldivers 2 stratagem codes, etc) onto that pad.

If you also play with a real controller, passthrough mode grabs it exclusively
and merges its input into the virtual pad, so the browser only ever sees one
gamepad.

While armed it also holds the keyboard backlight on -- the Dell firmware
dims it 10s after the last keystroke, and there are none while you play on
the pad ([backlight] in the config).

  hd2-macro install     config + systemd user unit + PATH symlink
  hd2-macro on|off|toggle|status
  hd2-macro run NAME    fire a macro via the running daemon
  hd2-macro devices     list gamepads and what the browser would see
  hd2-macro hide|unhide keep a physical pad out of the browser's gamepad list
  hd2-macro doctor      check permissions, joydev nodes, config
"""

